    "https://inside.southernct.edu/residence-life/student-employment": {
      "title": "Residence Life",
      "description": "Student Employment | Southern Connecticut State University Skip to main content Inside Southern Utility Nav SouthernCT.edu Calendar One Stop Main Menu Slide Toggle Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Search Search Slide In Main Menu About Admissions Academics Student Life Slide Menu Extra Map and Directions Directory Calendar News Athletics Library Inside Southern One Stop Alumni and Friends Slide Menu Bottom Apply Visit Give Search Toggle Residence Life Home Residence Life Student Employment Menu Residence Life About Reslife Communication Archive New Students Current Residents Room Selection Costs and Eligibility Apply for Housing Housing Cancellation Services Requests Meal Plans Housing Accommodations Housing Protocols Reserve Spaces Visiting a Resident Student Employment Contact Student Employment The Office of Residence Life provides employment opportunities for students during the academic year and summer months. Being a student employee in Residence Life is an amazing opportunity to get involved in the residence hall communities.  Being a student employee allows a person to grow personally, develop leadership skills, learn about teamwork, and work with our diverse residential student population.  It is also a fantastic opportunity to gain skills to work in a professional job environment. We offer a variety of different positions on campus including resident advisers, desk attendants, and summer student employees. Click on the positions below to learn more about our student employment opportunities. SCSU is an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer. The University seeks to enhance the diversity of its faculty and staff. Resident Advisor Senior Resident Advisor Desk Attendant Operations Assistant Programming Assistant Graphic Designer Computer Programmer Marketing Specialist Summer Associate Supervisor Summer Associate Summer Conference Assistant Connect With Us Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Footer menu Contact Us Work at Southern Footer 2 Menu Host an Event Library Footer 3 Menu Accessibility Website Feedback Footer 4 Menu Accreditation Title IX 501 Crescent Street, New Haven, CT 06515 (203) 392-SCSU © 2026 Southern Connecticut State University."
